{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city","id":769552,"title":"Dating the Oldest Stories - Enoch and the Second City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-19T14:31:06-08:00","id":769552,"title":"Dating the Oldest Stories - Enoch and the Second City","content":"Where do you put, in your personal opinion, the dates of Enoch and the Second City? Given that these topics are radically unclear and all supporting evidence is wildly contradictory of itself from the various sources?<br /> <br /> My thoughts, and I seek your own (and comments on mine)<br /> Enoch: Assuming that it existed and was destroyed by a flood, and that it was the source of (most) of the 3rd Generation - It seems to me that Enoch falls in either 14,000 BCE (Glboal Meltwater Pulse 1A) or 9,300 (Global Meltwater Pulse 1B). Im also assuming that 1.) No 4th Gens survive the flood, 2.) Embrace dates when possible are to be believed. Note this puts Set embraced long after the fall of Enoch. Assumption 1 is a bit of a mess, given Niktuku, etc... but I can live with it.<br /> <br /> [The Second City] We know that Japheth is the second or third child of Cappadocius, and is embraced in 7225. I doubt Cappadocius waited THOUSANDS OF YEARS after his siblings to start popping out childer, so again, our 4th gens are coming in the era of the second city. This puts the Second City founded around 7300 BCE at the latest. My best theory on its destruction is around 5600 BCE - later global meltwater pulse, possible [though not necessarily supported in archeology] sill-collapse flood event on the Black Sea and Persian Gulf. I like having the [Second City] be destroyed by a BLack Sea Flood, and spread out.. even as the Persian Gulf Flood drives the people who will be sumerians into the fertile crescent. Co-mingling of scattering 3rd and 4th gens gives us the confused mess that is early Cainite society after the second city.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9449-marcus-smythe","name":"Marcus Smythe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:44:09-08:00","id":769560,"title":"","content":"I put it at just over 5000 years ago. About 3200BC and just before the rise of the first Egyptian kingdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T15:20:45-08:00","id":769591,"title":"","content":"Coridan - so you just dismiss the older embrace dates, and such nigh-madness as the Genhenna book saying that the niktuku was 'more than twice as old' as Baba Yaga (herself already 7000)? How do you handle the biblical flood (or lack thereof) around 3000 BC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9449-marcus-smythe","name":"Marcus Smythe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T15:25:29-08:00","id":769594,"title":"","content":"Note.. the above is not intended at a criticism of your theory.. just thinking about how that all plays out... I suppose a lot of it is on how much your chronicle has to 'care' about all that stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9449-marcus-smythe","name":"Marcus Smythe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T15:34:17-08:00","id":769596,"title":"","content":"My dates are close to yours. I have the Second City fall around when the Gauntlet came up. Enoch, in my world, was there before the Fall, so things don't exactly line up with so much reality warping going on as the world Fell. But about 5500 BC is where I place the Second City, it was one of the first actual cities in the world, not counting the pre-Fall civilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T17:00:18-08:00","id":769642,"title":"","content":"I would definitely ignore embrace dates of anyone 4th gen or higher from pre 3000BC. Most historicity theories regarding the flood myth place it around that period of 2800-3200BC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T17:45:50-08:00","id":769674,"title":"","content":"I hold the &quot;real world&quot; of the World of Darkness has to take place after the end of the Ice Age, So 10,000 BC is the absolute oldest I go. However, I don't date the Flood to be purely a geological phenomenon. Although concepts like the Umbra, Gauntlet and such are not mentioned in Vampire, I hold the Antedeluvian world existed in a time when physical and spiritual reality were combined, so there isn't need for a worldwide Flood to happen in the physical world. It's an event whose evidence can't be detected by scientific means. The Fossil record is simply a conspiracy of the Technocracy to keep the truth from you.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The antedeluvians and/or their childer became the God Kings of Mesopotamian city states around 6000 BC or so, but prior to that they ruled together in the Second City aka Babel. So that's probably 8000 BC or so. By the time we get real historical and archaeological evidence of Sumeria in 5000-4000 BC, the Antedeluvians have likely exited open involvement and started hiding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T18:38:46-08:00","id":769707,"title":"","content":"I'm going with Black Fox. I wouldn't ignore the embrace dates, nor place them that recently in history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T21:49:02-08:00","id":769761,"title":"","content":"Taking all the general factors into consideration (most of the in-book sources, meshed loosely with Real World(tm) events -- but, as always, with the idea that &quot;if the supernatural is *real*, then much of history is most emphatically *NOT* what it appears to be...), I/most of those I've played with over the past 25 years date the &quot;First City&quot; as being before the meso-Atlantis era, or before 12,000BCE, back into a truly (M)ythic Era of history. When the Age of Leo came and went (approx. 10,000BCE, give or take) the &quot;Flood&quot; had already occurred, and over the millennia other &quot;cities&quot; developed. The Second City which was the &quot;last to fall&quot; (that is, be the point when shit hit the fan for the &quot;last time&quot; among the 3rd Gens) was circa 3,000BCE, which goes well in-hand with most book references.<br /> <br /> The real key to grasping how to (re)interpret all of the sources is to keep in mind that -- in all probability -- *most* of the stories/dates are <i>conceptually</i> true. That is, different events occurred at different times across many millennia, and just as in Real Life(tm) where various legends/myths arose and blended, melding into a &quot;history&quot; wherein something which had been passed on by word-of-mouth might thought to have occurred a few centuries ago actually has its roots stemming from *millennia* ago (and, occasionally, vice-versa), many of the seemingly &quot;sequential&quot; events in Cainite history are anything-but. The &quot;Caine&quot; and &quot;Lilith&quot; of &quot;proper&quot; Jewish lore (dating back approx. 6,000 years) are not, in all likelihood, the &quot;Caine&quot; and &quot;Lilith&quot; who are the progenitors of the vampires (and, in Lilith's case, a bunch of other critters, too). It's very easy for us, as readers/players, to too-quickly gloss-over certain aspects while analyzing this fictional setting, such as in this case in the assumption that the 3rd generation would move/act with a speed that mirrors our modern day sensibilities. Given the context of the narratives (and meta-narratives) involved, it's entirely plausible -- and, in fact, highly probable -- that the post-First City vampires could have <i>easily</i> spent millennia traveling, sleeping in torpor, plotting agendas that would take many centuries just to see begin to take shape, or spend an equal amount of time merely indulging in their desires/pursuits -- for god-like immortals, the passing of many centuries or even several millennia can be as how with mortals the passing of years or even decades can go in a blur, conceptually/cognitively.<br /> <br /> The time tables between the &quot;First&quot; and &quot;Second&quot; cities could very well have spanned a considerable number of millennia, and in all probability did. (There were, of course, many other cities/domains in the interim -- more, certainly, than had existed in the Real World(tm), given the existence of supernatural beings/powers, over that same time period -- so the title/attribution of &quot;Second City&quot;, even when kept solely in reference to the Ante's workings and ignoring humans/others, is simply that: a title/naming. Taking *any* of the concepts presented as stand-alone is, both in-narratively and more so meta-narratively, playing right into the hands of those blood-gods for whom a more &quot;simplified&quot;/occluded history works best for their manipulating/deceiving both their lineages as well as the broader world at large....) <br /> <br /> But anywho...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T21:53:40-08:00","id":769763,"title":"","content":"Adding an extra 3-5000 years to human civilization seems crazy to me. Eridu, the &quot;first city in the world&quot; was founded in 5400 BC, and would be the most likely candidate for Enoch. The city was abandoned some time between 3800 and 2900 BC, which fits in well with the theoretical times of the flood. I like it when things fit neatly into reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T22:15:15-08:00","id":769769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=769763#post769763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding an extra 3-5000 years to human civilization seems crazy to me. Eridu, the &quot;first city in the world&quot; was founded in 5400 BC, and would be the most likely candidate for Enoch. The city was abandoned some time between 3800 and 2900 BC, which fits in well with the theoretical times of the flood.<b> I like it when things fit neatly into reality</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... I suppose you do... (and somewhere, more than one Antediluvian smiles -- The Lie continues... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> The thing is, using Real World(tm) history as anything more than a general sounding board is asking for (meta-conceptual) trouble. In the WoD, magic is real (and something much more deep/esoteric than anything found in a Harry Potter book/movie); supernatural critters have been around for truly Mythic Ages(tm), influencing events since well before the last Ice Age (hell, it's all-but-stated that the Ananasi are responsible, in large part, for ending the Neanderthals approx. 30k years ago, via elimination and integration with the Ananasi-determined superior Homo Sapiens -- and other supers have had larger/wider influences than even that...); much of what humans *think* is their history is, in fact, often a conceptual forgery, particularly the further back over the millennia one goes. Even Real World(tm) archaeological data becomes of only middling narrative value considering that there are in-narrative factions/elements that have -- and continue to have -- manipulated historical information <i>across history</i>, including influencing (or outright forging/occluding) in-game research and studies to push various agendas, and on a level rivaling anything occurring in Real Life(tm), because again *supernatural forces are at work*.<br /> <br /> There is indeed, my dear Horatio, more to the WoD than you may yet dream... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T22:17:02-08:00","id":769771,"title":"","content":"Humans have been around a long, long, long time (Anatomically modern humans for around 100,000 years). Gobekli Tepe has been around since the 10th Mill. BC to the 8th Mil BC, and signs point to habitation. I fell comfortable point our Mythic Past farther in the, well, past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T02:08:50-08:00","id":769823,"title":"","content":"Here's what canon gives us:<br /> <br /> - Time of Thin Blood names the Antediluvians as more than ten thousand years old.<br /> - Japheth is Embraced in 7225 BCE. Clanbook Cappadocian says that Cappadocius never sired during the era of the Second City.<br /> - Rage Across Russia has Baba Yaga Embraced in 5000 BCE. By this point, the Second City is clearly over. Absimiliard disappears from history after his childe escapes his clutches, and finds purpose in hunting down his descendants to atone to Caine.<br /> - Nights of Prophecy says Vasilia is more than twice (!) Baba Yaga's age, putting her own Embrace at 12,000 BCE.<br /> - The Book of Nod states that the Fourth Generation did not exist until the Second City.<br /> - Clanbook Nosferatu says the Fourth Generation was around during the First City. So was the Matriarch to escape Absimiliard's clutches, who may or may not be Baba Yaga.<br /> - Clanbook Tzimisce puts the Embrace of numerous Fourth Generation Tzimisce before the Great Flood.<br /> - Clanbook Assamite gives a very extensive time frame for events in the Second City. Haqim settled there 100 years after its founding. 200 years later, the Baali appear. 100 years later, the Assamites/Salubri wipe them out. 500 years later, they return and ur-Shulgi is Embraced. 100 years later, they're beaten again, and the Second City starts to fall apart. That comes out to 1,000 years for its lifespan.<br /> <br /> As the OP says, canon is also a mess. Pick whatever dates you like, whether for the Second City's existence, the Embrace years of the oldest Methuselahs (Vasilia being twice Baba Yaga's age is one I'm happy to throw out), or simply the general order of events.<br /> <br /> So far as dates I'm a fan of, 10,000 BCE for the settlement of the First City, 6000 BCE for the Great Flood and foundation of the Second City, and 5000 BCE for the fall of the Second City. The end of the Ice Age nicely gels with Caine deciding it's time to end his self-imposed exile and rejoin civilization, and the Great Flood/Second City's founding (roughly) coincides with the 8.2 kiloyear event and start of agriculture in the Nile valley. This also fits with Gehenna placing the Second City in present-day Egypt: the Antediluvian god-kings needed food produced in outlying villages to support their city's mortal population. The Second City's fall 1,000 years occurs around the same time as the invention of the wheel and spread of symbols as proto-writing. Mortal survivors flee across the Middle East and bring remnant's of the city's (then for the time) advanced technology with them.<br /> <br /> In terms of age, that puts the (true) Antediluvians at 12,000 years old, ur-Shulgi and his Second City contemporaries (Yorak, the Dracon, Kartarirya) at 8,000-7,000 years old. It makes Japheth &quot;only&quot; seven thousand instead of nine thousand years old, but tough luck there, J.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, I see the era before the Great Flood as a time of unrestrained myth and wonder, when many of the rules that govern the contemporary World of Darkness aren't yet in place. There is no Gauntlet, no such thing as Paradox, the Shroud is all but nonexistent, Kindred clans effectively don't exist (each Antediluvian being a unique Kindred without childer), etc. The supernatural doesn't simply exist in harmony with the natural world, it governs its laws. By the time of the Second City, the Gauntlet and Shroud are up, Paradox is a minor problem for mages, and the Kindred are divided into clans. The supernatural still exists openly, but is no longer a seamless part of the world.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that between the Second City's fall in 5000 BCE and the appearance of writing in 3500 BCE, we have 2500 years of prehistory. That's a long, <i>long</i> time. The Antediluvians would've been as ancient during the fall of the Second City (5,000 years) as Baba Yaga was during the modern era. By the time writing is a thing, they have her beat at 7,500. I figure those 2500 between-years were a savage, barbaric age where the Third Generation freely sired, warred with, and diablerized one another and their progeny. A nightmarish era of non-stop Gehenna where the Fourth and Fifth Generations were used as cannon fodder by their infinitesimally older progenitors. There may well have been a number of now-extinct clans active during that period which didn't survive into the modern era; Gehenna's third scenario names a lot more than 13 Antediluvians as residents of the Second City. Some of the Third Generation may never have sired, but just as many (and the abortive clans they founded) may well have been wiped out during the Jyhad's brutal first battles.<br /> <br /> Also, I love Black Fox's explanation for the Great Flood and geological evidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T04:47:07-08:00","id":769860,"title":"","content":"I have Caine and Abel as mortals between 10 &amp; 9000 BC. They were farmers and that is the dawn of human agriculture. I don't think things need to be 100,000 years old to be ancient and mysterious. 12,000 is plenty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T05:13:03-08:00","id":769875,"title":"","content":"Well definitely 12,000 is plenty. I don't think anyone's saying they want 100,000 year old antediluvians. But 5,000 years seems a bit short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T05:31:18-08:00","id":769886,"title":"","content":"I appreciate everyone's thoughts. On the subject of 'things in the mythic age dont have to match real world dates' - I agree completely. I just like to tether things to real world dates where there seems to be a close enough fit and no reason to pick another date - the reason I went with (possible) historic flood events to tie to my enoch and second city is because the dates were close enough for government work, and there is no other controlling, or even particularly persuasive authority. And who is to say that our modern, technocratic explanations about ice sheet melting and rising global water levels is not just that.. a modern paradigm reflection of mythic era events.<br /> <br /> I agree, and like, the concept of making vampire generations and 'powers' to some degree map to changes in the underlying metaphysical nature of the world. Caine, his children, and grandchildren, lived in a much messier, less regimented, more magical world than their descendants. The difference between what we now call clans, or between mages and socerers, between generations - symptomatic of a decrease in the overall flexibility and 'magicalness' of the universe. Perhaps all the Weig got tied up as things were named, and order was forced on these beings. Maybe generation was not a thing before the 'fall of Enoch' era... or it was, but it was not FIXED (I like this interpretation). Perhaps the reason there are no '4th generations' from the first city is because, even if some of Enoch's survivors would have been of the 2nd, or 4th generations... at the time, age and magical power could raise generation, and there is no 'generation', in terms of power, beyond 3rd.. Caine just had more experience. Consider that even in the modern nights, magics exist which can raise generation without diablerie, either temporarily or permanently, and which can allow more than one cainite to benefit from a single soul.<br /> <br /> Im also contemplating that in my setting (such as it matters).. there WAS a cursed murderer figure, who was cursed by a great power, and driven out from a sacred place - who made some undead kids. The Hebrew Eden and Able and Caine story is a view on those events, informed by a religion that would not exist for thousands of years. However, not all vampires trace their line to that cursed first murderer figure... some of what we call the second generation may have been similarly created, or come from other lineages. The flood of Enoch simply ties up the lineages, leaving nothing surviving that had not reached the '3rd Generation' 10-dot apex of power... and saying they all come from the same vampire is just to put a bow on it.<br /> <br /> I also like set ACTUALLY being 'self-embraced' or cursed himself, and/or a god prior to this... at around 5000 BCE. Long after the end of the high magic era that gave us the first antedeluvians, but as a god-thing, Set retained enough of that early, universal 'weig' that he too appeared at the apex, or potential apex, of power... 10 dot maxima, 3rd generation. <br /> <br /> Final note, and I'm wandering here... as I see it, the difference between the 3rd generation and their childer consists of some sort of ineffable 'power' no longer present or possible in the world... which is why that last hurdle from 4th to 3rd is so hard (see poor Augustus and Tremere) is so difficult. Yet at the same time the nature of that power is nebulous... other than 10 dot potential and the fact of a LOT of age, the 3rd gens are not so markedly 'beyond' their children as to make any conflict meaningless. The Baba Yaga would probably lose a fight with Set... but he would know he had been kissed. 3 high-dharma Kuei-Jin fought a founder to a standstill... and he was likely older than all of them, put together. The difference between 4th and 3rd is mostly metaphysical, having to do with breadth of scope rather than focused power - and may have a transformational character, if you consider certain versions of the Gehenna story. Though I'm kinda meh on vampire that were having tea at 8000 years of age, and suddenly turn into tentacled murder-cities or subsume the very earth itself a relatively short 2K years later. Then again, I'm kinda meh on Vasilia totally annihilating the Baba Yaga as a standard action which did not provoke attacks of opportunity (I chock this up to writers wanting to show how awesome the niktuku is, and thus 'worfing' the poor little grandmother. The only reason that Ur-Shulgi breaking the Tremere Curse doesnt deeply annoy me is because my loathing for Clan Tremere could, if harnessed, remove the need for fossil fuels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9449-marcus-smythe","name":"Marcus Smythe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T05:57:15-08:00","id":769900,"title":"","content":"I only put the first city and the flood around then. I would say Caine cursed around 9500 BC, spends time with Lilith, then embraces the second and third gens around 7500 BC, and them they all start embracing around 5000 BC with the first city, but the flood kills all their initial childer and many other third gens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T15:26:47-08:00","id":770333,"title":"","content":"All references to &quot;weig&quot; in any vampire book should be ignored because it is ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T15:59:12-08:00","id":770352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=770333#post770333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All references to &quot;weig&quot; in any vampire book should be ignored because it is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of what was done with it is in fact ridiculous. But I find the idea of the wonder, the magic, the possibility of the universe calcifying into known, fixed, named things to be a resonant one. Even if the word was used (in vampire) for some dumb things, I think there was real possibility there, even if not always well executed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9449-marcus-smythe","name":"Marcus Smythe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T16:12:16-08:00","id":770362,"title":"","content":"Other WoD games have much better ways to describe it. &quot;Weig&quot; isn't about magic, possibility, or wonder, it's about making excuses to commit diablerie. The path of enlightenment that relied upon it as such was discredited within the game and replaced with more sensible paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T17:34:33-08:00","id":770396,"title":"","content":"In terms of the age of the antedeliuvians, it's important to make a distinction between their activity post-Flood and how long they may have existed before the Flood. The antedeluvians could have less than 10,000 years post-flood, and who knows how many beforehand.<br /> <br /> The antedeluvial world is something that is completely unknown and in fact unknowable to any Kindred. Whether it is the Biblical world (There were giants in the earth in those days), the Golden Age of Cronus/Saturn, Atlantis, the Hyborian Age, or something else is totally different than reality. I agree with False Epiphany that it is a time of unrestrained myth and wonder, or at least an Age undreamed of...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T18:15:08-08:00","id":770425,"title":"","content":"When I'm going to run a Vampire game (not a full world of darkness one) I normally go for christen science and go with the earth being about 6,000 years old, so adam and eve were made on the 7th day, so no one is older then them... at 5,999 years 359 days...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9055-gmforpowergamers","name":"Gmforpowergamers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T16:24:26-08:00","id":771039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=769875#post769875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well definitely 12,000 is plenty. I don't think anyone's saying they want 100,000 year old antediluvians. But 5,000 years seems a bit short.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Ravnos Antedeluvian has to be at least a million years old for him to be or Embrace Ravana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T18:23:25-08:00","id":771111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=771039#post771039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Ravnos Antedeluvian has to be at least a million years old for him to be or Embrace Ravana.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ravnos clanbook chapter that describes this event is called &quot;Agreed Upon Lies&quot; for a reason, no doubt. Plus it's ambiguous enough that Ravana the fourth generation Ravnos probably isn't Ravana the Yama King.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T23:25:33-08:00","id":771263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=771111#post771111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ravnos clanbook chapter that describes this event is called &quot;Agreed Upon Lies&quot; for a reason, no doubt. Plus it's ambiguous enough that Ravana the fourth generation Ravnos probably isn't Ravana the Yama King.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The whole setting is ambiguous however, IF the Ravnos antedeluvian is Ravana from the Ramayana or Embraced him then they existed in the Treta Yuga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T23:30:56-08:00","id":771265,"title":"","content":"I think it's more likely that the Ravnos antediluvian and his childer took on airs to justify themselves. Anyway, I don't think the antediluvian is ever presented as Ravana except <i>metaphorically</i> in visions during the Week of Nightmares. There's the methuselah named Ravana, but I think that neither he nor the antediluvian existed before Cainites existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:16:07-08:00","id":772981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus Smythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city#post769552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do you put, in your personal opinion, the dates of Enoch and the Second City? Given that these topics are radically unclear and all supporting evidence is wildly contradictory of itself from the various sources?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't try to date stuff from the Book of Nod. Might as well try to date stuff from other real world mythological sources. In my cWoD, the Book of Nod and it's event might have happened or they might not have happened. The whole system for counting generations might be a convenient fabrication, lies vampires have lived since times before the eldest cities or whatsoever. Same goes for my view on all other cWoD origin stories: they are myths that monsters tell themselves. Any embrace date before let's say 800 BCE is conjecture at best.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can point to Saulot, Tremere, Cappadocius and Augustus Giovanni as examples of active 3rd generation vampires. But are they? Is 3rd generation some arbitrary measure? I say it is, because we don't know about any 1st or 2nd generation vampires. All we know is that generation spreads out across roughly 12 steps (4th to 15th). The numbering of these steps is completely arbitrary and dependent upon the notion of Caine actually existing as... what? He isn't 1st generation, because the 1st generation would be one step <b>removed</b> from Caine. In the end, 3rd generation vampires are sometimes an observable phenomenon (at least if you are at the right time in the wrong place). Beyond that it's conjecture and fables.<br /> <br /> I know that the setting treats the antediluvians and the Caine mythology as objective truths (one of the greatest weaknesses of the whole setting). Heck, the largest and most successful vampire sect, the Camarilla, is founded on the believe that the antediluvians and Gehenna are myths! Yet, the setting proves them wrong time and time again. Nice way to underscore the bigotry of the Camarilla, but it's a disservice to the pillar of the setting. The Camarilla has always been the center piece of Vampire: <b>The Masquerade </b>(with that title, how could it be any different?), yet even the core rulebook always presents the Caine myth and generations as facts - instead of spending at least one paragraph to cast doubt on the whole story (hope V4 does with it's notion of Gehenna).<br /> <br /> I think in my V20 games from now on, the unspoken assumption will be: the Camarilla has it right, the Sabbat is a delusional sect of religious fanatics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:24:13-08:00","id":772986,"title":"","content":"I don't think generation means &quot;removed from Caine.&quot; I think it simply means number of generations, and Caine is the notional first generation, period. Not first generation <i>removed</i>, just first generation.<br /> <br /> I do agree that there's little to no certainty as to whether there was really a Caine and whether the third generation is really what vampires think they are or were, and there are certainly competing theologies at work as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:46:10-08:00","id":773007,"title":"","content":"Besides, Caine and the antes existed prior to the concept if zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:10:31-08:00","id":773123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=772986#post772986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think generation means &quot;removed from Caine.&quot; I think it simply means number of generations, and Caine is the notional first generation, period. Not first generation <i>removed</i>, just first generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote the Lexicon in V20:<br /> &quot;Generation: The number of \u201csteps\u201d <b>between a vampire and the mythical Caine</b>; how far descended from the First Vampire a given vampire is.&quot;<br /> <br /> Caine <b>cannot</b> be first generation, because Caine <b>cannot</b> be one step removed from himself. Someone even addressed that bit in Clanbook Toreador revised, but not in a satisfactory way.<br /> The concept about what a vampire is, really stems from observing the 4th generation, not the 3rd. The 3rd is by all accounts something else, because they are tremendously powerful compared to even the 4th generation. This is substantiated by the fact that all 3rd generation vampires you have &quot;died&quot; in the past 1000 years allowed themselves to die (Saulot wanted to be diablerized, same goes for Cappadocius, Tzimisce isn't as dead as everybody thinks, and Lasombra merged with the Abyss). Only exception is Ravnos, but he wasn't killed by another vampire, but by &quot;simply&quot; destroying him.<br /> <br /> As soon as you start stating the antediluvians by extending what we know about 4th generation vampires and their powers, they become riduculously killable (simply because they will start botching dice rolls...). <br /> <br /> So my thesis: whatever the 3rd generation are, they don't follow the normal rules for vampires. Vampires as the rulebook describes them only start to exist at an arbitrarily named &quot;4th generation&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:23:03-08:00","id":773140,"title":"","content":"The lexicon is wrong, then. The Book of Nod, the Ericyes Fragments, and multiple other sources establish Caine as the sire of the second generation, who sired the third generation, who founded the clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:33:14-08:00","id":773149,"title":"","content":"I guess that's one way to look at it. I don't think that an out-of-game source (Lexicon) is wrong. Rather the in-game sources that you cite are biased and thus wrong.<br /> <br /> BTW, this same definition of generation has been used as far back as 2nd Edition. Also, I am citing all this to cast reasonable doubt on the Caine-mythos and its whole baggage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","user":"Murder-of-Crows","date":". 11-24-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:33:57-08:00","id":773150,"title":"","content":"V20 page 27:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Caine, as the First Vampire, wandered the Land of Nod, where he eventually passed on his curse, Embracing those who would become known as the Second Generation. Their names are lost or vaguely known \u2014 the names most commonly agreed upon are Enoch, Irad, and Zillah \u2014 and they eventually begat the Third Generation, who would become the progenitors of what Kindred understand tonight as Clans. </div> </div> </div>V20 page 28:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The most widely acknowledged version of the Book of Nod claims the number of second Generation Kindred is three. In its chronicles, Caine Embraced these unknowable Ancients to dwell with him in his great city of Enoch and give him succor. </div> </div> </div>All of the setting material establishes Caine and his childer as such. The lexicon is wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:35:19-08:00","id":773153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=773149#post773149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that's one way to look at it. I don't think that an out-of-game source (Lexicon) is wrong. Rather the in-game sources that you cite are biased and thus wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is literally one source for your interpretation, and multiple sources for my interpretation. The lexicon is wrong and inconsistent with the setting material.<br /> <br /> The paragraphs I quoted above are precisely as IC or OOC as the incorrect lexicon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:47:28-08:00","id":773164,"title":"","content":"Okay, so your interpretation is right. Happy now? (I still believe the lexicon is the only correct source. Because otherwise generation doesn't make sense at all.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","user":"Murder-of-Crows","date":". 11-24-2015, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T09:28:35-08:00","id":773194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=773123#post773123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To quote the Lexicon in V20:<br /> &quot;Generation: The number of \u201csteps\u201d <b>between a vampire and the mythical Caine</b>; how far descended from the First Vampire a given vampire is.&quot;<br /> <br /> Caine <b>cannot</b> be first generation, because Caine <b>cannot</b> be one step removed from himself. Someone even addressed that bit in Clanbook Toreador revised, but not in a satisfactory way.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I know you are having an ongoing conversation already about this, but let me just jump in as one of the &quot;old school&quot;-guard to help clarify that particular point...)<br /> <br /> It's a compounded perceptual error -- the first occurring almost 25 years ago and the second occurring whenever someone (a reader) takes the applied use of the term out-of-context.<br /> <br /> When vampire first came out (1st Ed.), and in to some carry-over into 2nd, the term &quot;generation&quot; was *misused* by Mark and several others (that is, they misused the term as genealogically-used in The Real World(tm) when addressing Caine); this was actually addressed on the forums almost 20 years ago). On an in-narrative-cum-gaming-level, &quot;generation&quot; in the above cited usage was simply to indicate the number of steps from *the inception/creation of vampires*, with Caine being the &quot;first generation&quot; as he was the first vampire. The later, more commonly &quot;referenced&quot; use of (G)eneration incorporated two different applied definitions as if they were one. Again, a misuse of the term compared to real-life definitions. (Contextually, Caine is the 1st Generation when one considers Lilith to be his blood-creator, which she was according to most accepted in-narrative myths as most all of the various books agree that she is while albeit not always agreeing on how much of an influence she was/had over time.)<br /> <br /> Caine *is* &quot;the first generation&quot;, contextual to the setting and applied meanings. He *wouldn't* be if, say, this was all be kept track of by The Daughters of the Revolution, or similar real-life genealogical groups. But in this fictional setting, the double-meaning of the term stands and has been used in its seemingly contradictory manner for (in-narrative) many thousands of years and (meta-narratively) for almost 25 and across multiple editions/settings of the game. Much like with how words can often have self-contradictory meanings due to public-shift of word usage***, the term &quot;generation&quot; in Vampire has a different meaning than it does in conventional use.<br /> <br /> (***: It's like how &quot;figurative&quot; and &quot;literal&quot; have become mixed and cross-matched until now the two words have contradictory-yet-simultaneous meanings both for-and-against each other and themselves. Originally, &quot;figurative&quot; meant the actual physical manifestation of something -- the figure, as it were -- while &quot;literal&quot; meant the abstract concept/expression of something, the ideal rather than the concrete -- the literary concept of something. During the 19th century, however, the public -- particularly in America -- began misusing the two terms, crossing their meanings and applied uses, until by the 20th century their definitions became reversed from what they were. In recent decades, however, the two are now used in such a fluxed manner that in many cases only the context for when something is said indicates which definition should be applied/interpreted. (This means, funnily enough, that when younger people are &quot;corrected&quot; today for &quot;misusing&quot; the word &quot;literal-ly&quot;, those young people are actually using the original, proper definition of the word: when you say &quot;My head hurt so much, it *literally* exploded...&quot;, you *aren't* saying it physically exploded, but rather it hyperbolically did within a literary, abstract context. What all that has to do with this is to demonstrate that the shift in applied usage of a given word always has to be taken contextually with where/how it is used. Caine *is*, within the context of the game setting, the First Vampire and The First Generation Vampire (that is, the first &quot;generated&quot; vampire). Any seeming contradiction of usage is simply another case of &quot;figurative vs. literal&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Hope that helps....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":".  spacing 11-24-2015, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T09:42:52-08:00","id":773203,"title":"","content":"Indeed it helps, as I am familiar with all editions of the game except the first. <br /> <br /> I just add this from Clanbook Toreador revised (page 15): &quot;The First Generation was two, whose names are lost. They were the two perfect lovers, devoted to each other, and Caine hoped that by giving that love as a gift to eternity, he could mitigate the cruel deeds he had done in the past.&quot;<br /> <br /> This misuses generation even further, I realize. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T09:58:12-08:00","id":773214,"title":"","content":"Generation still denotes how far removed from Caine you are. 6th generation is 5 removed from Caine =p. <br /> <br /> The Toreador is a dope though, and says other dopey things in that section to drive the point home. I believe it was intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T10:15:07-08:00","id":773229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=773203#post773203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed it helps, as I am familiar with all editions of the game except the first.<br /> <br /> I just add this from Clanbook Toreador revised (page 15): &quot;The First Generation was two, whose names are lost. They were the two perfect lovers, devoted to each other, and Caine hoped that by giving that love as a gift to eternity, he could mitigate the cruel deeds he had done in the past.&quot;<br /> <br /> This misuses generation even further, I realize. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isnt that story something like:<br /> <br /> Caine, generation X, embraced The Lovers (gen X+1), who then offed themselves, and then Caine started again with Zillah, Enoch and Illyes (genx X+1), who then created the Antedeluvians (gen X+2).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:01:49-08:00","id":773361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=773203#post773203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed it helps, as I am familiar with all editions of the game except the first.<br /> <br /> I just add this from Clanbook Toreador revised (page 15): &quot;The First Generation was two, whose names are lost. They were the two perfect lovers, devoted to each other, and Caine hoped that by giving that love as a gift to eternity, he could mitigate the cruel deeds he had done in the past.&quot;<br /> <br /> This misuses generation even further, I realize. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>*Exactly*. By the time of the Revised books, it was an in-narrative-cum-meta-narrative &quot;point of order&quot;, as it were; what started out as a meta-narrative mistake eventually became used as an in-narrative &quot;stories-that-may-not-jibe&quot; (via stories that are, even to many of the most ancient vampires, myths that are not readily confirmable, and use terms in different contexts than used before or after). Also, it was a bit of a &quot;running joke&quot; at that point, both on the forums via the then-writers as well as at conventions where WW would be at. (Hell, I remember that being a &quot;wtf?&quot; question back at Masquerade II which was like '93 or '94... and the evading non-answer made everybody laugh...).<br /> <br /> Anywho...<br /> <br /> <br /> From the &quot;god POV&quot;, Caine *is* the &quot;first generation&quot; vampire (meaning, the first vampire &quot;generated/created&quot;); all other contexts are in-narrative distortions of myths told and re-told (and bastardized and outright lied about) over the course of many millennia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:36:02-08:00","id":773384,"title":"","content":"I bet the Bahari who think of Lilith as the first vampire would cackle at this sort of discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:53:33-08:00","id":773402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=773384#post773384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet the Bahari who think of Lilith as the first vampire would cackle at this sort of discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont evne the Bahari regard her as NOT a vampire, but more?<br /> <br /> Anyway, my copy of Reveleations of the Dark Mother should arrive tomorrow <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T14:24:32-08:00","id":773420,"title":"","content":"For my own games, Generation counts how many steps from Adam you are. Caine is the first Generation as he was the first man of woman born, thus the First Generation. Vampires are therefore counting their proximity in lineage to Adam, as Caines blood in their veins supersedes their mortal lineage.<br /> <br /> This means also that Caine, Abel and Seth, and their sisters if your using that version of the story, count as the First Generation. Problem solved for me anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T17:12:25-08:00","id":773521,"title":"","content":"As we all know, Peking Man was a vampire (per Dark Destiny*), and if we thus accept the premise that Caine was the first vampire and the rest of the mythohistory is not mere allegory etc, then Caine must have been created circa 700,000YA (years ago.) Clearly the real reason he and the antediluvians are beyond mortal ken is because they have never been human, and the weaknesses of the clans ultimately stem from being embraced from homo sapiens stock rather than homo erectus!<br /> <br /> <br /> (*it's actually a non-WoD story they threw in there because the editor thought it was awesome, and those early short story compilations aren't necessarily 'canon' anyway since they combined WoD with non-WoD freely. Homo Erectus Caine makes me laugh as a concept, though. The story itself is freely available these days here, if you want to give it a read: <a href=\"http://www.baenebooks.com/10.1125/Baen/F1597801569/F1597801569___8.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.baenebooks.com/10.1125/Ba...801569___8.htm</a> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T17:19:43-08:00","id":773524,"title":"","content":"It makes zero sense for Caine to be older than human agriculture =p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T17:39:10-08:00","id":773536,"title":"","content":"Well sure, but on the other hand, <i>homo erectus vampiricus</i>! If we do want to use the measure of 'no older than human agriculture' then we can potentially place Caine as far back as shortly before 23,000BC in the Levant, with that recent find in Galilee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T18:55:14-08:00","id":773571,"title":"","content":"You mean this?<a href=\"http://www.foxnews.com/science/2015/11/23/archaeologists-find-worlds-oldest-fava-seeds-at-site-in-galilee.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.foxnews.com/science/2015/...n-galilee.html</a> it says 10,000 years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:39:45-08:00","id":773593,"title":"","content":"I did a series of guesses a while back, about locating Caine and the Antediluvians (the latter sponsored civilizations in my concept) in time by assigning dates. Would this thread be interested?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:43:03-08:00","id":773598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=773384#post773384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet the Bahari who think of Lilith as the first vampire would cackle at this sort of discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go back in time, you have to reach a point where vampires did not use the Jewish mythology to describe the antedeluvian world. Classical era vampires in Rome probably referenced the Flood of Deucalion and the Golden Age of Saturn and ascribed the origin of vampirism in that world to some other murderous act (perhaps the Titans who dismembered and ate the flesh and blood of Zagreus?).<br /> <br /> However, by the time of the Middle Ages when both Christianity and Islam dominated the world from the Atlantic to the Indian Ocean, the references Childer and Fledglings knew was the Jewish myth. One can imagine an elder telling the stories of the origin of vampires to these neonates who kept referencing the only thing they knew about the antedeluvial world which was the story in Genesis: &quot;Oh, they survived the Flood of Noah. It must have been Cain who was the first vampire then.&quot; Rather than argue that this was not the myth told them back when Socrates was alive, they just agreed because they knew even by then, every culture kept substituting their own myths in describing the world before the Deluge.<br /> <br /> Likely, the exact story was codified by the early Camarilla in order to better create a common bond between the Kindred.<br /> <br /> It is easy to forget how ancient the world really is. To the Romans, the time of Egypt and Sumeria was older to them, than the Roman Empire is old to us. A lot gets lost in the transmission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:43:57-08:00","id":773600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeebers76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=773593#post773593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a series of guesses a while back, about locating Caine and the Antediluvians (the latter sponsored civilizations in my concept) in time by assigning dates. Would this thread be interested?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please post them. I think such sharing is relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T20:14:12-08:00","id":773605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=773571#post773571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean this?<a href=\"http://www.foxnews.com/science/2015/11/23/archaeologists-find-worlds-oldest-fava-seeds-at-site-in-galilee.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.foxnews.com/science/2015/...n-galilee.html</a> it says 10,000 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and generally I don't get my archaeology information from <i>Fox news</i>. The site in question - Ohalo II, while that article talks about Ahihud - is 13,000 years older. In addition, human agricultural practices are probably older still, but didn't develop into recognizable forms - hunter-gatherers planting fruit trees and coming back years later doesn't scream 'cultivation' but is distinctly human and likely a very old practice of ours, at least if you listen to the agriculture historians - until relatively late in its practice as we began to permanently settle down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/science/2015/jul/24/archaeologists-find-possible-evidence-of-earliest-human-agriculture\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/82a553fb2b62db1328530aa5f4cdc148bc128737/0_193_5400_3240/master/5400.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;quality=85&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;precrop=40:21,offset-x50,offset-y0&amp;overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&amp;overlay-width=100p&amp;overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdGctYWdlLTIwMTUucG5n&amp;enable=upscale&amp;s=d6c6bf9adfa622486f97329d37887779\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/science/2015/jul/24/archaeologists-find-possible-evidence-of-earliest-human-agriculture\" target=\"_blank\"> Archaeologists find possible evidence of earliest human agriculture </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/science/2015/jul/24/archaeologists-find-possible-evidence-of-earliest-human-agriculture\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.theguardian.com/science/2015/jul/24/archaeologists-find-possible-evidence-of-earliest-human-agriculture </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Study of plant remains on shores of Sea of Galilee show crop cultivation may have developed 23,000 years ago </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2015/07/150722144709.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.sciencedaily.com/images/scidaily-icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2015/07/150722144709.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> First evidence of farming in Mideast 23,000 years ago </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2015/07/150722144709.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2015/07/150722144709.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Until now, researchers believed farming was &amp;apos;invented&amp;apos; some 12,000 years ago in an area that was home to some of the earliest known human civilizations. A new discovery offers the first evidence that trial plant cultivation began far earlier -- some 23,000 years ago. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T00:35:32-08:00","id":773707,"title":"","content":"Now, all of this is pure speculation, so don't throw a fit if it doesn't adhere to canon.<br /> <br /> Caine\u2019s murder of Seth is probably a reference to the extinction of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_heidelbergensis\" target=\"_blank\">Homo heidelbergensis</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_rhodesiensis\" target=\"_blank\">Homo rhodesiensis</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_neanderthalensis\" target=\"_blank\">Homo neanderthalensis</a> and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_antecessor\" target=\"_blank\">Homo antecessor</a> by Homo Sapiens Sapiens (either that, or it\u2019s a reference to organized warfare, which dates to 14,000BC). The \u201cAntediluvians\u201d are approximately 77,000 years old (at most). The oldest human civilization (as we define the term), dates back 5,100 years ago in Egypt, which is 100 years older than Mesopotamia. Ironically, none of the clans who claim to be the first of the 3<sup>rd</sup> Generation are likely candidates, despite their respective ego. I\u2019ve based this hypothesis on the origins of their various cultural names. I figure that some of these individuals subsumed various cultural identities over the thousands of years, some of which might predate their introduction to a given society. I also am deliberately linking werewolves into the Biblical cosmology. This is due to the evidence presented in Devil\u2019s Due, the Demon Dark Ages book, and because honestly I don\u2019t particularly like the concept of fanatical environmentalist warriors being crossed with the concept of werewolves. There\u2019s no basis for it in any occult legend I have ever read or heard of, and it sounds pretty farfetched. You will also note that the 2<sup>nd</sup> generation doesn\u2019t necessarily conform to what you and I would think of as the game rules, as they spawned other supernatural races than Cainites.<br /> <br /> 1<sup>st</sup> Gen<br /> Caine<br /> <br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> Gen<br /> As far as anyone knows, the 2<sup>nd</sup> Generation was murdered by the 3<sup>rd</sup> Generation. Sometime afterward, each of the Antediluvians wandered off to embed themselves into different cultures.<br /> Zillah: Sekhmet, a fierce huntress who guarded the pharaoh and controlled diseases<br /> Irad the Strong (mortal name Mehujael)<br /> Enoch the Wise/Lawgiver<br /> Jabal<br /> Tubal (Xue)<br /> Adah (Gaia)<br /> <br /> This is the rough order, based upon age of the parent civilizations, listing first the second generation progenitor, and then the Antediluvian offspring. It\u2019s likely that the Cappadocian progenitor is the oldest out of the 3<sup>rd</sup> Generation, despite other clans\u2019 claim to the contrary.<br /> <br /> <b>Egypt</b> Zillah the Beautiful/Sekhmet (apparently Caine liked \u2018em predatory) 3100bc<br /> Tzimisce, Lasombra, Absimillard (Nosferatu), Haquim(Assamites)<br /> <br /> <b>Mesopotamia (Sumeria),</b> Enoch the Wise/Lawgiver 3000bc<br /> Arikel(Toreador), Malkav(Malkavians), Illyes (Brujah), Saulot(Salubri), Osiris/Sargon of Akkad (Cappadocians, probably the oldest of the Antediluvians)<br /> <br /> <b>India</b> Jabal 3000bc<br /> Veddhartha(Ventrue), Zapathusura(Ravnos)<br /> <br /> <b>Peru </b>Adah (female) 2500bc<br /> Gaians (shapechangers), Adah basically became Luna/Gaia. Yup, they\u2019re NOT as old as they think they are. This is confirmed by demons (Devil\u2019s Due). Native to the New World, but many migrated to Africa, Europe, and Asia. Note that the current theory is that Europeans introduced the concept of werewolves to the New World, so this assessment is purely fictional of course, it\u2019s just the best I can come up with and still have Garou be relatively old as a race.<br /> <br /> <b>Central Asia</b>, Irad the Strong aka Mehujael 2000bc<br /> Ennoia(Gangrel), Set(Setites)<br /> <br /> <b>China </b>Tubal (Xue) 1750bc<br /> Kuei-jin, aka Chinese vampires, had approximately 5 disciples who later became the Quincunx.<br /> <br /> 3<sup>rd</sup> Gen<br /> <b>Assamites</b>: Haquim, he invested in the Middle Eastern peninsula (Persians).<br /> <b>Brujah</b> (female): Brujah (Greek Athenian) who was originally a 4<sup>th</sup> gen of Illyes, (male) who himself was a Greek Spartan. Illyes diablerized Troile. Note that Celerity came first, not Temporis. Eventually became the Phonecian Carthaginians, because she was pissed that the Greeks fell and the Romans took over. Brujah eventually invested in Portugal and Spain, not just Greece, once Carthage was razed.<br /> <b>Cappadocians</b>: Cappadocius/Osiris, Originally Egyptian (competed with Set), but gave up on them for the Hittites/Turks after Egypt fell. However, he never invested as much effort into a civilization again. Prefers to enter any culture that has a significant amount of death worship, like Venice, New Orleans, Mexico\u2019s Day of the Dead, Egyptian pyramids, the catacombs in Rome, etc. Became very Italian later.<br /> <b>Followers of Set</b>: Originally a somewhat decent person who saw what Cappodocius had created, and wanted it. Lasombra wanted Egypt as well, so he began corrupting Set at the same time Cappodocius gave up on Egypt. Despite Set\u2019s devolving ethics, he entrenched himself in Egypt which frustrated Lasombra into leaving for the Minoans. Set arrived in Egypt with the Hyksos invaders, as their deity. Later on he became ever more evil, and was demonized by the Egyptian culture. Soon after, Shaitan (Baali, 4<sup>th</sup> Generation childe of Set) was sired. During the height of Egyptian power, Shaitan diablerized Set.<br /> <b>Gangrel</b> (female): Ennoia, controlled the Scandinavians/pagan Europeans<br /> <b>Lasombra</b>: Angra Mainyu/Apep, Competed with &amp; corrupted Set for Egypt during the Hyksos invasion, but later gave up for the Minoans who became the Sea Peoples. They in turn became the Spanish.<br /> <b>Malkavians</b>: Malkav (male), very Babylonian, but his childer migrated all over Europe and Russia.<br /> Followers of Set/Setites: Set (himself corrupted by Lasombra) aka Hyksos invader of Egypt<br /> <b>Nosferatu</b>: Absimillard. His childe the Matriarch, a 4<sup>th</sup> Gen, liked the Southern Germans in particular, but she didn\u2019t really invest in a people, as she wandered to the largest human cities. Cripples and social reject/survivor types.<br /> <b>Ravnos</b>: Zapathasura, got into the Indian Romani migration into Europe. In 1099 Jerusalem, Zapathasura was diablerized by Tremere. In many ways, he is Rakshasa.<br /> <b>Salubri</b>: Saulot, the monotheistic religions instead of a specific people. They end up influencing much of the medieval and Renaissance Church, displacing the Lasombra (the latter is far too fractious).<br /> <b>Toreador</b> (female): Arikel/Ishtar/Aphrodite/Astarte who will eventually become French/Gallics<br /> <b>Tremere</b>: Austrians, and invested most spectacularly in Hitler and the Nazis.<br /> <b>Tzimisce</b>: The Eldest adopted the European Slavs/Rus.<br /> <b>Ventrue</b> (female): Veddhartha, an Indian, who liked the Indus river valley types, then ancient Romans (then Holy Roman Empire, then Germans). Basically she followed the \u201cpower groups\u201d to a certain extent.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T12:31:13-08:00","id":774196,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in the bit from <i>Devil's Due </i>you mentioned. You have a page number(s) I can go look it up on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:10:37-08:00","id":774350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=774196#post774196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in the bit from <i>Devil's Due </i>you mentioned. You have a page number(s) I can go look it up on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 28, under The Warders Prophecy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T16:32:43-08:00","id":776874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=773598#post773598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go back in time, you have to reach a point where vampires did not use the Jewish mythology to describe the antedeluvian world. Classical era vampires in Rome probably referenced the Flood of Deucalion and the Golden Age of Saturn and ascribed the origin of vampirism in that world to some other murderous act (perhaps the Titans who dismembered and ate the flesh and blood of Zagreus?).</div> </div> </div> </div>QFE. I always figured that Caine was identified with Ixion way back when, with the Kindred as a whole calling themselves Ixionidae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T07:14:48-07:00","id":1454520,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't go so far. If we want to have some historical accuracy even knowing that the lore is deliberately written in a vage, obscure and inconclusive to create a mistery I would use some criteria to narrow down the possibilities.<br /> <br /> I start with the time line of human condition (<a href=\"https://www.southampton.ac.uk/~cpd/history.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.southampton.ac.uk/~cpd/history.html</a>).<br /> Around 10.000 BCE we are moving from hunting nomads behaviour to farming settlements.<br /> <br /> The part below is from <a href=\"https://www.history.com/topics/pre-history/fertile-crescent\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.history.com/topics/pre-h...rtile-crescent</a><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> The Fertile Crescent around 9000 BCE had began to practice agriculture by domesticating sheep and pigs around 11,000 to 9,000 B.C.<br /> Domesticated plants, including flax, wheat, barley and lentils, first appeared around 9,500 B.C.<br /> <br /> One of the oldest known Mesopotamian cities, Nineveh <b>(a)</b> (near Mosul in modern Iraq), may have been settled as early as 6,000 B.C. Sumer civilization arose in the lower Tigris-Euphrates valley around 5,000 B.C <b>(b)</b>.<br /> <br /> The origins of Sumer civilization are debated, but archaeologists suggest Sumerians had established roughly a dozen city-states by the fourth millennium B.C., including Eridu and Uruk in what is now southern Iraq.<br /> <br /> Sumer is the earliest known civilization in ancient Mesopotamia and may have been the first human civilization anywhere in the world. They called themselves the Sag-giga, the \u201cblack-headed ones.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ancient Sumerians were among the first to use bronze. They pioneered the use of levees and canals for irrigation. Sumerians invented cuneiform script, one of the earliest forms of writing. They also built large stepped pyramids called Ziggurats.<br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> The First city is placed around the crescent fertile and it is described as an exiting important city. The tale follows and Cain arrives at this city. Therefore we must rule out anything that comes before 9000 BCE because the tale tells about a very import and big city.<br /> <br /> The reasoning goes on. It is said that Cain when arrived at this city, later referenced as Enoch, had been wandering around and might have visited the Sumerians and brought back some technology from that people. Well, assuming this is true we narrow down even further the possibilities and rue out anything before the Sumer civilization, so nothing before 6000 BC. The next exclusion is due the fact that the Sumer civilization must be already there sometime in order to develop knowledge.<br /> <br /> It is not a strong rule and this can be overlooked but to develop technology nowadays we rely on language to formalize the knowledge so others can read and understand what to do. If we assume that this was a sine-qua-non condition than we must accept that cuneiform written was present at 3400 BCE (oldest tablet found so far) <b>(c).</b><br /> - If we don't overlook the writing requirement than it is possible to accept that Cain was around the Sumerian cities somewhere between 4500 BC ( from (b) ) and 3400 (b) and brought what he learned to this city later known by the WW Lore as Enoch.<br /> - If we overlook than Cain returns from the Sumerians after 3400 BCE.<br /> <br /> Now we have one thing to assume. The city was there before Cain and it was bug for the standards by that time. So maybe it was settled around the same time as Nineveh, meaning 6000 BCE.<br /> The city becomes The First City after Cain arrives and rules it. So it might be happened:<br /> Hypothesis1 - somewhere between 4500 BCE ( from (b) ) and 3400 BCE (b) OR<br /> Hypothesis2 - close as possible from 3400 BCE<br /> <br /> The WW Lore also tells us that this city was destroyed by the Deluge. But it is unclear what deluge is the one. The WW Lore from (<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Deluge\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Deluge</a>) gives us:<br /> - Genesis Flood Narrative - Great Flood to circa 2350 BCE<br /> - Black Sea Deluge - plausible inspiration to circa 5600 BCE<br /> <br /> If we established that the First City as the Lore now defines was destroyed by a Flood than we must rule out the Black Sea Deluge from 5500/5600 BCE.<br /> It induces us to conclude that Cain ruled from 4500 BCE until 2350 BCE OR, at least from 3400 BCE till 2350 BCE depending on what hypothesis are we assuming to be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3082-dfcastro","name":"dfcastro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T08:00:32-07:00","id":1454525,"title":"","content":"Fun Fact: This thread is older than 3 of the Antediluvians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T14:17:20-07:00","id":1454609,"title":"","content":"I think D:tF solves the issue of dating the first and second city briliantly. Demons and angel were able to reshape time/space/reality, so the events of Caine's curse, his pact and then betrayal of Lilith and the foundation of the First City are all &quot;beyond time&quot; as we know it. Then came the deluge or the reshaping of time and reality after Lucifer lost. The First City was destroyed and the Second Generation founded the Second City. In this period time was still malleable and fluid, and other realms exixted as well (the reign of Osiris in Egypt for Example), but it slowly solidified in what we know today, when it did, not long after the abandonment of the Second City due to caine's wrath vampires &quot;emerged&quot; into the current timeline, around 3000 BC.<br /> As for werewolves, they remember a completely different timeline because it happened in a diverget reality that was shaped into the current one as well.<br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> <br /> I do not consider &quot;To Grandmother's House&quot; canon in any way. Besides being a crappy railroad (one where you are literally a spectator in your own adventure) those dates don't make sense and are there only to justify the finale, not because the author had an insight into the secret history of the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T20:34:34-07:00","id":1454636,"title":"","content":"I agree with Haquim, though I would put the date further back than 3K BCE. In short, you cannot nail to a specific date when Cainites entered the scene. Also, I don't think Caine or the Antediluvian were literate or bothered writing their stories down. Others did that for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T13:01:27-07:00","id":1454706,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d personally set the Flood at about 12,900 years ago to align with the Younger Dryas comet impact theory and similarly tie the First City to an Atlantis situated at the Eye of the Sahara (which back then was a tropical savanna with lakes and streams) that lies just south of the Atlas Mountains (and is also where the historian Heroditus placed Atlantis).<br /> <br /> It should be noted that the actual story of Atlantis didn\u2019t include any sort of superscience... they were considering an advanced civilization because they had agriculture, architecture, astronomy and an organized religion. Also worth noting is that Atlantis was just the capital and the king Atlas divided the realm up between his ten male heirs.<br /> <br /> Just a bit of stretching and you could make that 13 heirs and say what mortals call \u201cAtlantis\u201d was actually the First City and survivors carried the stories to Egypt where they were recorded (note too that Egyptian mythology says they were originally a colony established by a great power to the West).<br /> <br /> When one considers the technological backslide of the Bronze Age collapse (we still can\u2019t decypher Linear A because literally nothing yet found that could translate it has survived) you could conceivably drop a Neolithic or early bronze age civilization in c. 14-15k year ago that was wiped out by the flood accompanying the Younger Dryas comet impact c. 13k years ago and humanity basically had to rebuild from there finally getting back on track about the time of the earliest Levantine, Egyptian and Indian settlements.<br /> <br /> Throw in Neanderthal* werewolves who once hunted Humanity to near extinction c. 50-60k years ago until we finally found an edge that could fight them (vampires? ghouldom?) and you\u2019ve got yourself a greatest hits of Cryptohistory.<br /> <br /> * <a href=\"https://treeofwoe.substack.com/p/when-orcs-were-real\" target=\"_blank\">https://treeofwoe.substack.com/p/when-orcs-were-real</a> (they use orc, ogre and boogeyman and even link it to our ancestral fear of the dark, but in WoD cosmology I can\u2019t help but think of the Garou Impergium and that one of their intermediate forms is said to resemble a Neanderthal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T13:19:29-07:00","id":1458401,"title":"","content":"The Second City was built on the ruins of the First, I believe and the Second City was located on the outskirts of todays Cairo. Several WW products mention this. We can date the end of it due to the multiple sources we have about the early years of Set. It fell around 3100 BC. According to kindred history it lasted a long time though. Cairo by night mentions that the desiccation of the Sahara was due to the presence of so many Antediluvians in such a small area.<br /> <br /> The end of the last Saharan humid phase was about 4000 BC with an abrupt shift into hyper-arid about 3500 BC. This would indicate that the stories of kindred managing to exist in harmony for millennia are exactly as false as they sound. the Second City seems to have lasted about 500 years before the younger kindred rebelled and tried to consume their elders.<br /> <br /> Now, there was a phase between the First and Second city. If we assume that the same parasitical desiccation occurred during the First City as well, the last African Humid Phase started about 10 000 BC. That would date the fall of the First City about even with phase I of Gobekli Tepe. It does give us a 6000 years long interval between the First and Second city. That may be too long, I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T20:54:46-07:00","id":1458447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=1458401#post1458401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Second City was built on the ruins of the First, I believe and the Second City was located on the outskirts of todays Cairo. Several WW products mention this. We can date the end of it due to the multiple sources we have about the early years of Set. It fell around 3100 BC. According to kindred history it lasted a long time though. Cairo by night mentions that the desiccation of the Sahara was due to the presence of so many Antediluvians in such a small area.<br /> <br /> The end of the last Saharan humid phase was about 4000 BC with an abrupt shift into hyper-arid about 3500 BC. This would indicate that the stories of kindred managing to exist in harmony for millennia are exactly as false as they sound. the Second City seems to have lasted about 500 years before the younger kindred rebelled and tried to consume their elders.<br /> <br /> Now, there was a phase between the First and Second city. If we assume that the same parasitical desiccation occurred during the First City as well, the last African Humid Phase started about 10 000 BC. That would date the fall of the First City about even with phase I of Gobekli Tepe. It does give us a 6000 years long interval between the First and Second city. That may be too long, I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>First city was Pre-Flood though and there was a global 100m rise in sea levels at the end of the last Ice Age, c. 11,000 BC that, not coincidentally coincide with both the supposed destruction of Atlantis and the timing giving for various flood myths in other cultures around the world. There's some evidence that a silt dam may have initially held some of the global sea level rise back in the Mediterranean basin until it gave way and caused a much more rapid rise that would have flash flooded many regions that were coastal and the time and left them under dozens and eventually hundreds of feet of water.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is that, at least for VtM, the First City was the origin of the Atlantis myth (an advanced for its time city lost in a flood) and dated to the end of the last Ice Age with the Second City being formed somewhere along the Nile and reigning throughout the pre-Dynastic period until finally falling in the period before the rise of the first historic Pharaoh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T05:55:27-07:00","id":1458496,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3082-dfcastro\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3082_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3082\" data-vbnamecard=\"3082\">dfcastro</a>, I found your post very interesting, but I have to add some points.<br /> <br /> Several 4th generation vampires are given likely dates of Embrace between 4000 BCE and 5000 BCE. And there is no reason to think that older cities can't have existed in the WoD than Nineveh and not have been found by human archaeology yet, even been rendered impossible to find and date due supernatural intervention.<br /> <br /> Even being conservative, I think the Deluge of the First City could have been, indeed, the Black Sea Deluge. That would destroy some early cities with maybe a few centuries, enough to be big and important and developed in comparison at such a time. It could be that Nineveh or some slightly older city was around by 6000 BCE, and Caine got knowledge from there, then brought to the First City and it was razed by the flood around 5600 BCE.<br /> <br /> Four hundred years is a short time for modern Kindred standards, but there was no Kindred standards at the time. Caine's rule would become legendary no matter what because it was, after all, the First City. The entire chronology of it fits easily in one human lifetime, 400 is plenty. Writing definitely isn't a requisite for technology, this is a disregard to the technological development of early humans. You need a lot of technology to build a city to begin with, and that was definitely an older achievement than writing. The Greeks had a 400 period without any writing system and no ability to read the writings from previous people, and yet retained their ability on metallurgy, ship building and several others during this period, even if not everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/769552-dating-the-oldest-stories-enoch-and-the-second-city?p=1454706#post1454706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* <a href=\"https://treeofwoe.substack.com/p/when-orcs-were-real\" target=\"_blank\">https://treeofwoe.substack.com/p/when-orcs-were-real</a> (they use orc, ogre and boogeyman and even link it to our ancestral fear of the dark, but in WoD cosmology I can\u2019t help but think of the Garou Impergium and that one of their intermediate forms is said to resemble a Neanderthal).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note, there are reasons for this to be a fringe theory. And by the way, recent genetic findings revealed that we did'n mixed with Neanderthals by our women mating with their males, it was the opposite at least 4 out of 5 times. It seems like our ancestors had a thing for pretty Neander flowers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid